they could spend the money meant for highways, a new mass transit options, new subway lines, for example. This was unprecedented. No state had ever reallocated money like this. It was a laboratory for what could happen when the narrative changed and the orthodoxy of highways was questioned. At the end of it, Sergeant scheduled a broadcast slot to announce his final decision. Governor's Transportation Message video taken 4 424, air date 1130-72. Did you know what he was going to say? No, we were all lobbying like crazy, but, you know, we didn't know.
可以把原本用于高速公路的资金花在新的公共交通选择上，例如新的地铁线路。这是前所未有的。没有任何一个州以这种方式重新分配过资金。这是一个实验室，展示了当叙事发生改变、高速公路教条受到质疑时会发生什么。在此结束时，萨金特安排了一个广播时段来宣布他的最终决定。州长交通信息视频拍摄于4月24日，播出日期1972年11月30日。你知道他要说什么吗？不，我们都在疯狂地游说，但是，你知道的，我们不知道。

